# PART 1: MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise Coverage

MITRE ATT&CK has 15 Enterprise tactics. Here is PHANTOM's honest coverage:

| # | Tactic | PHANTOM Coverage | Missing |
|---|---|---|---|
| TA0043 | **Reconnaissance** | 60% | Shodan/Censys APIs, crt.sh, email harvesting, LinkedIn OSINT, favicon hashing |
| TA0042 | **Resource Development** | 5% | Infra setup, fake identity provisioning, domain purchase, cert acquisition |
| TA0001 | **Initial Access** | 40% | Phishing infra, USB drops, watering hole, supply chain, VPN bruteforce |
| TA0002 | **Execution** | 35% | LOLBAS abuse, WMI exec, scheduled tasks, mshta/regsvr32/certutil living-off-land |
| TA0003 | **Persistence** | 10% | Registry run keys, scheduled tasks, WMI subscriptions, DLL hijacking, startup folder |
| TA0004 | **Privilege Escalation** | 25% | winPEAS/linPEAS partial, missing token impersonation, UAC bypass, kernel exploits |
| TA0005 | **Stealth / Defense Evasion** | 5% | AMSI bypass, ETW patching, process hollowing, timestomping, log clearing |
| TA0112 | **Defense Impairment** | 0% | AV/EDR kill, Defender exclusion abuse, audit log manipulation |
| TA0006 | **Credential Access** | 30% | Has hashcat/john, missing LSASS dump, Kerberoast, AS-REP roast, DPAPI, DCSync |
| TA0007 | **Discovery** | 40% | Has nmap/enum4linux, missing Seatbelt host enum, AD enumeration, cloud asset discovery |
| TA0008 | **Lateral Movement** | 5% | Missing Pass-the-Hash, Pass-the-Ticket, RDP, WinRM, DCOM, SCM lateral movement |
| TA0009 | **Collection** | 5% | Missing keylogging, screenshot, clipboard monitor, browser credential dump |
| TA0011 | **Command & Control** | 15% | Has Metasploit shells, missing proper C2 (Sliver/Havoc/Cobalt Strike), DNS C2, HTTPS malleable |
| TA0010 | **Exfiltration** | 5% | Missing data chunking, DNS exfil, HTTPS exfil, steganography exfil |
| TA0040 | **Impact** | 5% | Missing ransomware sim, data wipe, service disruption, log destruction |

**Average MITRE ATT&CK coverage: ~20%**

