# PART 2: Post-Exploitation — The Biggest Gap

This is where PHANTOM is most critically behind. After getting a shell, real operators use:

## 2A. Host Enumeration (What Seatbelt Does — PHANTOM Has NONE of This)

Seatbelt (GhostPack) runs 80+ checks on a compromised host:

| Category | Checks PHANTOM is Missing |
|---|---|
| **AV/EDR Detection** | AMSI providers, Windows Defender config, AppLocker rules, Sysmon presence |
| **Credential Hunting** | DPAPI master keys, Windows Vault, credential manager dump, KeePass files |
| **Browser Data** | Chrome/Firefox/Edge saved passwords, cookies, history, bookmarks |
| **Cloud Creds** | AWS `~/.aws/credentials`, Azure tokens, GCP auth files on disk |
| **Network Intel** | ARP table, DNS cache, TCP/UDP connections, mapped drives, network shares |
| **Persistence Points** | AutoRuns, scheduled tasks (non-Microsoft), WMI subscriptions, registry run keys |
| **AD Context** | LAPS config, NTLM settings, Kerberos tickets, domain trusts |
| **Juicy Files** | PowerShell history, SSH private keys, PuTTY saved sessions, FileZilla creds |
| **Token Info** | Current privileges (SeDebugPrivilege, SeImpersonatePrivilege), token groups |
| **LOLBAS** | Living-off-the-land binaries present on host that can be abused |

**Fix:** PHANTOM needs a `host_enum` module that runs the equivalent of `Seatbelt -group=all` on Linux AND Windows targets.

---

## 2B. Credential Access — PHANTOM Has 30%, Needs 100%

What real operators extract:

### Windows Credential Sources (ALL MISSING from PHANTOM):
```
LSASS memory dump → sekurlsa::logonpasswords (Mimikatz)
SAM database → reg save HKLM\SAM
NTDS.dit → DCSync (domain controller only)
DPAPI → master keys → browser passwords, credential manager
Kerberos tickets → klist / Rubeus dump
LSA secrets → service account passwords
Chrome/Firefox → encrypted SQLite → decrypt with DPAPI
KeePass .kdbx → extract + crack
Windows Credential Manager → cmdkey /list
Wi-Fi profiles → netsh wlan show profile ... key=clear
```

### Linux Credential Sources (PARTIALLY in PHANTOM):
```
/etc/shadow → john/hashcat ✅ (PHANTOM has this)
SSH private keys (~/.ssh/id_rsa) ❌
.bash_history / .zsh_history → plaintext passwords ❌
Docker secrets / env files ❌
Git credential store (~/.git-credentials) ❌
AWS/GCP/Azure credential files ❌
Application configs (database.yml, .env, config.php) ❌
```

