These are the bread and butter of internal AD pentesting:

| Attack | Tool | PHANTOM Status |
|---|---|---|
| **Kerberoasting** | Rubeus, Impacket GetUserSPNs | ❌ Missing |
| **AS-REP Roasting** | Rubeus, Impacket GetNPUsers | ❌ Missing |
| **Pass-the-Hash** | Impacket, NetExec pth | ❌ Missing |
| **Pass-the-Ticket** | Rubeus ptt | ❌ Missing |
| **Overpass-the-Hash** | Rubeus asktgt | ❌ Missing |
| **Golden Ticket** | Mimikatz golden | ❌ Missing |
| **Silver Ticket** | Mimikatz silver | ❌ Missing |
| **DCSync** | Mimikatz lsadump::dcsync | ❌ Missing |
| **Shadow Credentials** | Whisker | ❌ Missing |
| **Constrained Delegation** | Rubeus s4u | ❌ Missing |
| **RBCD Attack** | StandIn, Get-RBCD-Threaded | ❌ Missing |
| **Certificate Abuse (ESC1-ESC8)** | Certify, Certipy | ❌ Missing |

**Active Directory Certificate Services (ADCS) is the #1 internal pentest finding in 2024-2025.**
ESC1-ESC8 attacks let you go from low-priv user to Domain Admin via misconfigured certificate templates.
PHANTOM has zero coverage of this.

