# PART 3: Defense Evasion — PHANTOM Has Almost Nothing

This is the most critical gap for red teamers. Getting a shell is useless if EDR kills it.

## 3A. AMSI (Anti-Malware Scan Interface) Bypass
Every PowerShell payload PHANTOM generates will be caught without AMSI bypass.

```powershell
# Basic bypass patterns (ALL missing from PHANTOM):
[Ref].Assembly.GetType('System.Management.Automation.AmsiUtils').GetField('amsiInitFailed','NonPublic,Static').SetValue($null,$true)
# Patching amsi.dll in memory via reflection
# Matt Graeber's 1-line bypass
# Hardware breakpoint based bypass
# Memory patching via P/Invoke
```

## 3B. ETW (Event Tracing for Windows) Blind
ETW captures everything PowerShell does. Operators patch it:
```csharp
// Patch EtwEventWrite to return immediately — MISSING from PHANTOM
// This blinds Defender, SentinelOne, CrowdStrike telemetry collection
```

## 3C. Process Injection Techniques (ALL MISSING)
| Technique | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Classic DLL Injection | Inject shellcode via WriteProcessMemory + CreateRemoteThread |
| Process Hollowing | Replace legitimate process memory with payload |
| Process Doppelgänging | Use NTFS transactions to hide payload |
| APC Queue Injection | Queue shellcode via NtQueueApcThread |
| Module Stomping | Overwrite a loaded DLL's .text section |
| Thread Hijacking | Suspend thread, redirect RIP, resume |
| Heaven's Gate (WoW64) | Bypass 32-bit hooks by calling 64-bit syscalls directly |
| Direct Syscalls | Bypass userland hooks entirely (SysWhispers2/3) |
| Indirect Syscalls | Use ROP gadgets to reach syscall instruction |

## 3D. Payload Delivery Evasion (ALL MISSING)
| Technique | Tool | What it Does |
|---|---|---|
| AMSI bypass loader | `AmsiScanBufferBypass` | Patches AMSI before payload runs |
| ETW bypass | `EtwBypass` | Blinds event tracing |
| Shellcode obfuscation | `donut`, `sgn` | Converts .NET → shellcode, encodes it |
| PE obfuscation | `ConfuserEx`, `Themida` | Obfuscates .NET assemblies |
| EDR unhooking | `Freshycalls`, `SysWhispers3` | Removes userland hooks |
| Signed binary proxy | `LOLBAS` techniques | Uses `mshta`, `regsvr32`, `certutil`, `wscript` |
| In-memory execution | Reflective DLL loading | Never touches disk |
| Fileless malware | WMI subscriptions, registry | Persists without exe on disk |

