# PART 4: Web Application — Remaining Deep Gaps

## 4A. Business Logic Flaws (Requires AI Reasoning — Only PHANTOM Can Solve This)
No scanner finds these automatically. Examples from real H1 reports:
- Negative quantity in cart → negative charge to card
- Coupon code applied unlimited times (race condition)
- Password reset doesn't invalidate old sessions
- Email change doesn't require password confirmation
- Insecure direct object reference on invoice download (`/invoice/1234`)
- Price manipulation via parameter tampering in checkout
- Account enumeration via password reset timing difference

**PHANTOM's AI layer is UNIQUELY positioned to test these — no other OSS tool can.**

## 4B. Advanced Injection Techniques Missing
| Attack | Tool Needed | Current Coverage |
|---|---|---|
| SSTI (Server-Side Template Injection) | `tplmap`, manual | Nuclei templates only |
| CRLF Injection | Manual payloads | Nothing |
| HTTP Parameter Pollution | Manual | Nothing |
| Path Traversal (advanced) | `dotdotpwn` | Nothing |
| Open Redirect Chains | Manual + nuclei | Partial |
| Host Header Injection | Manual | Nothing |
| Subdomain Takeover | `subjack`, `can-i-take-over-xyz` | Nothing dedicated |
| Clickjacking | X-Frame-Options check | Nothing |
| Content-Type sniffing | Manual | Nothing |
| WebSocket Vulnerabilities | Manual + Burp | Nothing |
| XMLRPC attacks | `xmlrpc-brute`, manual | Nothing |
| Insecure File Upload | Custom payloads | Nothing |

## 4C. Subdomain Takeover — HIGH VALUE, MISSING
One of the easiest critical findings in bug bounty:
```bash
# Tools PHANTOM needs:
subjack -w subdomains.txt -t 100 -timeout 30 -ssl
can-i-take-over-xyz  # checks 100+ services
dnsx -l subdomains.txt -cname  # find dangling CNAMEs
```
Services vulnerable to takeover: GitHub Pages, Heroku, Shopify, Fastly, AWS S3, Azure, etc.

## 4D. Prototype Pollution — Growing Attack Surface
```javascript
// Payloads PHANTOM doesn't test:
?__proto__[admin]=true
?constructor.prototype.admin=true
// In JSON bodies:
{"__proto__": {"admin": true}}
// In URL-encoded:
foo[__proto__][admin]=true
```
`ppmap` and `semgrep` rules needed to detect this server-side and client-side.

