# PART 5: OSINT — Only 50% Covered

## What Top Bug Bounty Hunters Actually Use for OSINT:

| Tool/Technique | What It Finds | PHANTOM Status |
|---|---|---|
| **Shodan** | Exposed services, versions, vulnerable ports across all IPs | ❌ No API |
| **Censys** | Like Shodan but certificate-first | ❌ No API |
| **crt.sh** | SSL cert transparency → subdomain discovery | ❌ Missing |
| **VirusTotal** | Passive DNS, historical subdomains, relations | ❌ Missing |
| **URLScan.io** | Historical screenshots, DOM, requests of any URL | ❌ Missing |
| **Wayback Machine** | Historical endpoints, old JS files with leaked keys | ❌ Missing |
| **FOFA / ZoomEye** | Chinese Shodan alternatives (finds things Shodan misses) | ❌ Missing |
| **hunter.io / apollo.io** | Employee emails from company domain | ❌ Missing |
| **LinkedIn OSINT** | Org chart, tech stack from job postings | ❌ Missing |
| **GitHub Dorking** | Leaked secrets, internal code, API keys | ❌ Missing |
| **Google Dorks** | site:, inurl:, intitle:, filetype: chains | ❌ Missing |
| **ASN Lookup** | Find all IP ranges owned by target company | ❌ Missing |
| **favicon hashing** | Find hidden assets by favicon hash on Shodan/Censys | ❌ Missing |
| **Reverse WHOIS** | Find all domains registered by same person/org | ❌ Missing |

### GitHub Dorking — Fastest Secrets Source
Real methodology used by top hunters:
```
org:targetcompany password
org:targetcompany api_key
org:targetcompany secret
org:targetcompany BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY
org:targetcompany .env
org:targetcompany aws_access_key_id
filename:.npmrc _authToken
filename:docker-compose.yml password
```
Tools: `truffleHog`, `gitleaks`, `gh-dorks`, `gitdorker`

### Favicon Hash Recon (Missing from PHANTOM)
```python
import requests, mmh3, codecs
response = requests.get('https://target.com/favicon.ico')
favhash = mmh3.hash(codecs.lookup('base64').encode(response.content)[0])
# Search Shodan: http.favicon.hash:{favhash}
# Finds ALL servers using this favicon → internal/staging apps exposed
```

